{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119952","id":3784069014,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7hjE-W","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119952","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119952.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119952.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119952","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119952/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119952/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119952/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f0317a5f23ab30c1ed10c5efdaf7a32c21b72703","number":119952,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Generalize `OPCODE_TYPE_ADJUST_*`","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThe GDScript VM has a set of opcodes `OPCODE_TYPE_ADJUST_*` for calling specializations of the `VariantTypeAdjust::adjust()` template method for each `Variant` type:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d569fcf207aea355ea9d0822255ad490945f5572/core/variant/variant_internal.h#L978-L983\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d569fcf207aea355ea9d0822255ad490945f5572/core/variant/variant_internal.h#L960-L967\r\n\r\nHowever, there is already a non-template `VariantInternal::initialize()` method that does the same thing (except for checking the `Variant` type):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d569fcf207aea355ea9d0822255ad490945f5572/core/variant/variant_internal.h#L58-L62\r\n\r\nSo, we can reduce the number of opcodes. This is primarily to reduce the boilerplate. This could also potentially reduce the size of `GDScriptFunction::call()` (if the C++ compiler doesn't optimize it). Furthermore, of all the `OPCODE_TYPE_ADJUST_*` opcodes, only the ones for `Object`, `Array`, and `Dictionary` are currently used (plus possibly packed arrays, but I couldn't reproduce it). For this reason, the typos fixed in #119844 do not cause errors.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nCurrently, `write_type_adjust()` is only used to initialize temporaries in optimized opcodes (it could be replaced with `write_construct()`, but `VariantInternal` likely allows for runtime optimizations). Perhaps we should check the management of temporaries for reference types to avoid double cleanups (at the beginning and end).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":27909808